course: dictionary
lesson: 3424
title: Extinct: gone for good
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Extinct is a science word, and you will meet it in many lessons. An extinct animal or plant no longer exists anywhere in the world, because every last one has died. «Dinosaurs, dodos and mammoths are extinct.» You cannot find a living one anywhere.
explain: Extinct can also describe a volcano that will never erupt again, or a custom, job or language that is no longer used. Use the context clues to tell which meaning you need. «The black-footed ferret was thought extinct until a dog found one in Wyoming in 1981.» The words «thought» and «until» are the clues: the ferret was not really gone, people just believed it was.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you say «The paddlefish is extinct, so we can see one at the zoo», the sentence stops making sense, so extinct must mean that no living ones are left anywhere.
fact: Extinct means that a kind of animal or plant no longer exists anywhere in the world.
fact: «Extinct» can also mean a volcano that will never erupt again, or a job, custom or language that is no longer used.
fact: Phrases to know: become extinct, go extinct, extinct species, extinct volcano.
fact: «Thought extinct» means people believed a kind of animal had died out, but it was still alive somewhere, as with the coelacanth.
fact: Endangered animals can become extinct if people do not protect them.
exercise: «Dinosaurs, dodos and mammoths are extinct.» What does extinct mean? | Sleeping deep under the sea | Very rare and hard to spot | Found only in zoos | *No longer exists anywhere in the world
exercise: «The coelacanth was thought extinct for 66 million years.» What does the word thought tell you? | Scientists proved it had died out | It was a brand new animal nobody had named | *People believed it had died out, though it had not | It was very big and very heavy
exercise: Which word in «Megalodon is extinct: no fresh teeth, bitten whales or sightings are found» means no longer living? | teeth | *extinct | sightings | whales
test: Ben says, «The paddlefish is extinct, so we will see one at the zoo.» What is wrong with his sentence? | Extinct means it lives under the water only | *Extinct means no living ones exist anywhere, so the zoo cannot have one | Extinct means very big, so it would be easy to see | Extinct means it sleeps all day
test: Which sentence uses extinct to mean a volcano that will never erupt again? | The volcano erupted last summer and everyone ran. | We climbed the volcano to see the view. | *The old volcano is extinct and will never erupt again. | The volcano is sleeping and may wake up soon.
exam: «The black-footed ferret was thought extinct until a dog found one in Wyoming in 1981.» Which words show it was not truly gone after all? | was thought | in Wyoming | in 1981 | *until a dog found one
